{
  "about": "About",
  "aboutSubtitle": "The story and purpose behind Rafeeq",
  "aboutTagline": "Your Muslim Companion",
  "aboutBeginningTitle": "How Rafeeq began",
  "aboutBeginningBody": "Rafeeq began with a simple idea from my elder brother. We are both software developers, and one day he decided to build an Islamic app that would bring essential Muslim needs such as the Qur'an, Qiblah, prayer times and more together in one place. Later, I — Muzamil Ghafoor — joined him, and Rafeeq became a journey shared by two brothers.",
  "aboutTogetherTitle": "Growing together",
  "aboutTogetherBody": "Since then, my brother and I have worked on Rafeeq as a team. We started again together, gradually implemented the core features and kept adding more over time. Whenever our other responsibilities leave us some time, we come back to Rafeeq to improve it and thoughtfully prepare the next update.",
  "aboutDesignTitle": "Our design journey",
  "aboutDesignBody": "When we first started, we did not have a complete design plan. Even after adding features, we often felt that something was still missing, so we rebuilt the app's entire design system twice. With this latest version, we have tried to create something minimal, clear and pleasantly refined. The Islamic app Sadiq was also a meaningful source of inspiration for us, and I am grateful for it.",
  "aboutUmmahTitle": "For the Ummah",
  "aboutUmmahBody": "For me, Rafeeq is more than just another software project. My brother and I want to keep improving it for the Ummah of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH). I am deeply thankful to Allah Almighty for giving us the ability to work on something that may benefit other Muslims.",
  "aboutFreeTitle": "Free for life, In Sha Allah",
  "aboutFreeBody": "I want Rafeeq to remain free for everyone for its entire lifetime, In Sha Allah. In the future, we may add an optional way for Muslims to support the app's development and running costs. Any support will be used to maintain and improve Rafeeq; we do not intend to take anything from it for ourselves, In Sha Allah.",
  "aboutCommunityTitle": "We are here for you",
  "aboutCommunityBody": "My brother and I are here for you. You can request a feature, report a bug or share an idea with us. We will listen, and we will keep doing our best to make Rafeeq better for Muslims everywhere.",
  "aboutClosingStatement": "Built by Muslims, for Muslims — for the Ummah of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) and for the sake of Allah Almighty. ❤️ ",
